ze-selector='false' data-show-column-explorer='true' data-show-chart-builder='true' data-row-headers='[]' data-hidden-columns='[]' data-has-stable-row-id='false' data-lazy='false' data-preload='false'></marimo-table></marimo-ui-element><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Hardware:</strong> 2 x A10G, 24GB, 600 GB/s. <strong>Budget:</strong> 12 phase-1 trials, 3 slots per round.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Note the pairing: <strong>model_a</strong> takes long prompts and short answers (prefill heavy); <strong>model_b</strong> takes short prompts and long answers (decode heavy). They stress different parts of the device, which is what makes the consolidation question interesting rather than obvious.</span></span></div>"
